#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161812 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162020 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c029623-354f-5800-ac1b-05681ed7ff2f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability at a Single Point"}] :question/id #uuid "0a247025-c5ec-5b0d-a741-4eaceee20b57" :question/math-academy-id "e-8462" :question/problem "Given that $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 21 \\right\\rbrace$, compute $P(X = 18)$." :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S$, then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{\\begin{vmatrix}S &},\\end{vmatrix}x ∈ S; 0, \\mid otherwise\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nX \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 21 \\right\\rbrace\n$$\n\nand the set\n\n$$\nS = \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 21 \\right\\rbrace\n$$\n\nhas\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid S &= 21 - 7 + 1 = 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nitems. So, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{15},\\begin{vmatrix}x = 7, 8, 9, …, 21 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X = 18) = f(18) = \\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161813 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162021 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "adf7ba0e-5e16-52c3-af7d-b51a311b11fa" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "884ee1a6-a5e3-5e50-b975-71167ebd923e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8463" :question/problem "Given $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 16\\right\\rbrace$, compute $P(8 \\leq X < 13)$." :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S$, then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{\\begin{vmatrix}S &},\\end{vmatrix}x ∈ S; 0, \\mid otherwise\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nX \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 16 \\right\\rbrace\n$$\n\nand the set\n\n$$\nS = \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 16 \\right\\rbrace\n$$\n\nhas\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid S &= 16 - 7 + 1 = 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nitems. So, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{10},\\begin{vmatrix}x = 7, 8, 9, …, 16 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nIn $S$, there are $5$ items $(8, 9, 10, 11, 12)$ that satisfy\n\n$$\n8 \\leq X < 13\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(8 \\leq X < 13) = 5 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{10} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161829 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162036 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3148b483-52f4-5740-bd82-194aab44f89a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "36688142-f65d-50a0-8454-fe6315617283" :question/math-academy-id "e-8565" :question/problem "Given $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 14 \\right\\rbrace$, compute $P(X \\geq 9)$." :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S$, then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{\\begin{vmatrix}S &},\\end{vmatrix}x ∈ S; 0, \\mid otherwise\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nX \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 14 \\right\\rbrace\n$$\n\nand the set\n\n$$\nS = \\left\\lbrace 5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 14 \\right\\rbrace\n$$\n\nhas\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid S &= 14 - 5 + 1 = 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nitems. So, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{10},\\begin{vmatrix}x = 5, 6, 7, …, 14 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nIn $S$, the items that satisfy\n\n$$\nX \\geq 9\n$$\n\nare $9, 10, 11, \\ldots, 14$. There are\n\n$$\n14 - 9 + 1 = 6\n$$\n\nof these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 9) = 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{10} = \\dfrac{3}{5}\n$$"}]}
